content.thinking:
Progress: the note text is now accurate ("die Karte bleibt beim zuletzt gezeigten Ausschnitt stehen" — so `shifted` was true), but my new assertion `outsideNote.pane2.startsWith(paneTwoBefore)` fails: pane 2's src *did* change (from `…/full/349/…` to `…/652,/…1904/…`).

Why? Sequence with the Denmark pair:
- The panes start with `cvv`-restored? No: fresh `?cmp=` link, no cvv → whole sheets. But wait — the *device-local* cvv state may persist? `cvv` is URL state only, and the local list doesn't include cut-outs. Hmm.
- Press 1: propagates → Denmark keeps... the readout says "Ausschnitt 7578×1904 von 7578×6984" → so pane 2 DID move to a band on press 1 (the shared area = Denmark's whole box, mapped to the whole sheet, then reshaped to the stage aspect → band, i.e. a *cut-out* per the viewer's own bookkeeping).
So pane 2's src changes on press 1 (from full to band), and later presses give 'outside' without further changes. My assertion compared pane2's src *before the first press* — wrong premise (the pane legitimately followed once before leaving the extent).

Fix the assertion to what actually matters: after the note appears, pane 2 must NOT have followed the *latest* cut-out. That's hard to detect without a reference. Practical approach: capture pane 2's src right before the final press that produced the note... complexity.

Better: assert on the pair where the *first* propagation is already outside. That happens when the source's window after one press leaves the target extent: with the globe (window after 1 press: ±110° lon, ±56° lat) and a target at lat 62+ (Svalbard/Scandinavia) or lon > 110. There might not be such a record.

Alternative, simpler and still meaningful: assert that pane 2's region is *unchanged between two consecutive presses* (i.e. it stops following) — measure pane 2's src before a press and after it, when coverage is 'outside'. Implement: after the note appears, read pane2 src; press `+` once more on pane 0; wait ~1.5s; read pane2 src again; assert equal, and assert the note is still shown. That's a clean assertion: "once the cut-out has left the sheet, further zooms do not move it, and the note stays".

Let me restructure the block:
```js
    // Two presses further: the pane must not follow into the wrong place, and the note stays.
    const paneTwoAtNote = outsideNote?.pane2 ?? '';
    await cdp.pressKey('+', { keyCode: 187 }); await sleep(1200);
    await cdp.pressKey('+', { keyCode: 187 });
    const afterLeaving = await cdp.waitFor(`(() => { const note = document.querySelector('[data-compare-coverage="1"]'); const img = document.querySelectorAll('#compare-view-body .app-viewer__image')[1]; if (!note || note.hidden) return ''; return { pane2: img?.src || '', note: note.textContent, state: document.querySelector('#compare-sync-hint')?.textContent || '' }; })()`, {timeout: 8000}).catch(() => null);
    check(
      '...',
      Boolean(outsideNote) && /ausserhalb dieses Blattes/.test(outsideNote.note) && outsideNote.borderLeft === '4px' && /Gesamtansicht|Ausschnitt/.test(...) && Boolean(afterLeaving) && afterLeaving.pane2 === paneTwoAtNote && /ausserhalb der belegten Ausdehnung/.test(afterLeaving.state),
      ...
    );
```
The core: note + 4px bar + the pane's image unchanged across two further zoom steps, and the hint naming the outside case.

Let me rewrite the assertion part accordingly.

